{
  "slug": "whitepaper-writing",
  "concept": "Whitepaper Writing",
  "generated": "2026-09-08",
  "summary": "A whitepaper is a long-form, authoritative B2B document that educates a business reader on a problem and positions a solution.",
  "facets": [
    {
      "title": "Overview",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "A whitepaper is a long-form, authoritative B2B document that educates a business reader on a problem and positions a solution.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/whitepaper-writing/#overview",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Lighter than academic: persuasion is allowed; citation density is moderate; the author has a point of view.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/whitepaper-writing/#overview",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Heavier than a blog post: data and methodology are visible; claims are sourced.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/whitepaper-writing/#overview",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Length: 8–20 pages typical; 8–12 is the sweet spot for engagement.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/whitepaper-writing/#overview",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Voice: third-person company-as-narrator.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/whitepaper-writing/#overview",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Gordon Graham identifies three structural types:",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/whitepaper-writing/#overview",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Backgrounder: explains a technology, methodology, or product in depth.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/whitepaper-writing/#overview",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Numbered-list: \"5 Reasons to Adopt X,\" \"10 Pitfalls of Y.\"",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/whitepaper-writing/#overview",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Problem/solution: describes an industry-wide problem, evaluates current solutions, presents a new approach.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/whitepaper-writing/#overview",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "1. The problem → solution → proof → CTA arc",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "The arc is inverted from a sales pitch: a pitch starts with the product; a whitepaper ends with the product.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/whitepaper-writing/#1-the-problem-solution-proof-cta-arc",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "2. Executive-summary discipline",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "1–2 pages, no more.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/whitepaper-writing/#2-executive-summary-discipline",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "States the problem, the proposed solution, the most compelling proof point, and the call to action.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/whitepaper-writing/#2-executive-summary-discipline",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Stands alone.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/whitepaper-writing/#2-executive-summary-discipline",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Written last, after the full paper is drafted.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/whitepaper-writing/#2-executive-summary-discipline",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "3. Vendor-neutral vs sponsor-disclosed tone",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Vendor-neutral rules:",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/whitepaper-writing/#3-vendor-neutral-vs-sponsor-disclosed-tone",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Name the problem before naming the product.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/whitepaper-writing/#3-vendor-neutral-vs-sponsor-disclosed-tone",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Discuss competing approaches honestly; their drawbacks should be real, not strawmen.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/whitepaper-writing/#3-vendor-neutral-vs-sponsor-disclosed-tone",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Cite third-party sources for problem-scoping statistics.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/whitepaper-writing/#3-vendor-neutral-vs-sponsor-disclosed-tone",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Use the sponsor \"About\" block as the only place where company puffery is acceptable.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/whitepaper-writing/#3-vendor-neutral-vs-sponsor-disclosed-tone",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "A whitepaper that reads as a thinly disguised sales pitch is rejected by 60% of B2B decision-makers.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/whitepaper-writing/#3-vendor-neutral-vs-sponsor-disclosed-tone",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "4. Citation density and source hygiene",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "The right citation density is 2–6 cited claims per page.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/whitepaper-writing/#4-citation-density-and-source-hygiene",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Source hierarchy (descending credibility):",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/whitepaper-writing/#4-citation-density-and-source-hygiene",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Peer-reviewed academic research and government data",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/whitepaper-writing/#4-citation-density-and-source-hygiene",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Major analyst firms (Gartner, Forrester, IDC, McKinsey)",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/whitepaper-writing/#4-citation-density-and-source-hygiene",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Standards bodies (NIST, ISO, IEEE, W3C)",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/whitepaper-writing/#4-citation-density-and-source-hygiene",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Industry surveys with disclosed methodology and sample size",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/whitepaper-writing/#4-citation-density-and-source-hygiene",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "The sponsor's own anonymized data (acceptable for proof sections)",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/whitepaper-writing/#4-citation-density-and-source-hygiene",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "The \"verify the verifiable\" rule: every claim of the form \"X% of organizations report Y\" must cite a source the reader can access.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/whitepaper-writing/#4-citation-density-and-source-hygiene",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "6. The \"case study within a whitepaper\" pattern",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Embed a real (or anonymized) customer story in the proof section:",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/whitepaper-writing/#6-the-case-study-within-a-whitepaper-pattern",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Challenge → Approach → Result structure (mini case study)",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/whitepaper-writing/#6-the-case-study-within-a-whitepaper-pattern",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "One direct customer quote, attributed",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/whitepaper-writing/#6-the-case-study-within-a-whitepaper-pattern",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Two-to-three quantified outcomes",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/whitepaper-writing/#6-the-case-study-within-a-whitepaper-pattern",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "7. Length and design budget",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "8–12 pages: standard problem/solution",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/whitepaper-writing/#7-length-and-design-budget",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "12–16 pages: technical or research-heavy",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/whitepaper-writing/#7-length-and-design-budget",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "16–20 pages: research-grade with original primary data",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/whitepaper-writing/#7-length-and-design-budget",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "20+ pages: split into a series",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/whitepaper-writing/#7-length-and-design-budget",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Design budget: Branded title page, table of contents (clickable PDF), 2–4 charts/infographics minimum, pull quotes every 2–3 pages, case-study sidebar boxes.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/whitepaper-writing/#7-length-and-design-budget",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "8. Gated vs ungated",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Gate when: Original research with high differentiation value; mid-or-bottom-funnel audience.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/whitepaper-writing/#8-gated-vs-ungated",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Ungate when: Foundational education; high SEO value; technical and form-allergic audience.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/whitepaper-writing/#8-gated-vs-ungated",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Hybrid pattern (modern best practice): First 2–3 pages ungated, full PDF gated behind a form.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/whitepaper-writing/#8-gated-vs-ungated",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
